From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Beri <jmberi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libm: build every long double source with CMake

The CMake build lists the long double sources in newlib/libm/ld by hand,
and six that the meson build compiles are missing: s_finitel.c,
s_fpclassifyl.c, s_getpayloadl.c, s_issignalingl.c, s_scalbl.c and
s_significandl.c. picolibc's own <math.h> calls __fpclassifyl for
fpclassify(), isnan() and friends on a long double, so a CMake-built
library that a long double reaches -- libc++'s, for one -- does not link.

Add them, so both builds provide the same functions.
---
 newlib/libm/ld/CMakeLists.txt | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/newlib/libm/ld/CMakeLists.txt b/newlib/libm/ld/CMakeLists.txt
index 38a8a5b35..4fc05ec36 100644
--- a/newlib/libm/ld/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/newlib/libm/ld/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -80,12 +80,16 @@ picolibc_sources(
   s_cosl.c
   s_fabsl.c
   s_fdiml.c
+  s_finitel.c
   s_fmal.c
   s_fmaxl.c
   s_fminl.c
+  s_fpclassifyl.c
   s_frexpl.c
+  s_getpayloadl.c
   s_isinfl.c
   s_isnanl.c
+  s_issignalingl.c
   s_llrintl.c
   s_llroundl.c
   s_logbl.c
@@ -93,9 +97,11 @@ picolibc_sources(
   s_lroundl.c
   s_rintl.c
   s_roundl.c
+  s_scalbl.c
   s_scalbln.c
   s_scalbnl.c
   s_signbitl.c
+  s_significandl.c
   s_sincosl.c
   s_sinl.c
   s_tanl.c
